1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,970
The president stops breathing.

2
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:04,250
One second ago, he was laughing.

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:07,830
Now he's gripping the table,
his face changing color.

4
00:00:08,180 --> 00:00:09,210
You step forward.

5
00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:10,530
Across the room,

6
00:00:10,660 --> 00:00:14,310
six guards reach for their
weapons because five minutes ago,

7
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:16,380
you were the person who
handed him that drink.

8
00:00:16,420 --> 00:00:17,810
"Freeze."

9
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:22,530
You have spent three years
preparing to save this man's life.

10
00:00:22,880 --> 00:00:26,650
Nobody prepared you for what happens
if saving him makes you look guilty.

11
00:00:28,260 --> 00:00:29,430
Three years earlier,

12
00:00:29,480 --> 00:00:32,890
you arrive wearing a suit that
costs more than your father's car.

13
00:00:33,220 --> 00:00:34,410
The suit is free.

14
00:00:34,760 --> 00:00:38,530
So is the apartment, the driver,
your mother's medical treatment.

15
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:42,780
Your younger brother has suddenly been
accepted into a university that rejected

16
00:00:42,820 --> 00:00:43,750
him twice.

17
00:00:44,060 --> 00:00:45,750
Your family calls it a miracle.

18
00:00:45,980 --> 00:00:48,290
The government calls it
your benefits package.

19
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:51,790
You have been selected to
protect President Viktor Saran,

20
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:56,420
a man who has won four elections and
somehow never appeared on a ballot beside

21
00:00:56,460 --> 00:00:57,650
anyone interesting.

22
00:00:57,960 --> 00:00:59,270
Your job sounds simple.

23
00:00:59,620 --> 00:01:01,570
Stand close. Pay attention.

24
00:01:01,820 --> 00:01:04,010
If something happens, move first.

25
00:01:04,540 --> 00:01:06,620
The head of security, Colonel Marek,

26
00:01:06,660 --> 00:01:10,150
walks you through a palace with
enough marble to bankrupt a mountain.

27
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:12,610
He stops outside the president's office.

28
00:01:12,860 --> 00:01:14,690
"Three rules," he says.

29
00:01:14,940 --> 00:01:16,370
"Don't repeat what you hear.

30
00:01:16,620 --> 00:01:18,790
Don't mistake friendliness
for friendship."

31
00:01:19,100 --> 00:01:20,390
He straightens your tie.

32
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:24,530
"And if you see something unusual,
tell me before you tell anyone else."

33
00:01:24,940 --> 00:01:27,230
You ask what counts as unusual.

34
00:01:27,600 --> 00:01:28,650
Marek looks at you.

35
00:01:28,880 --> 00:01:29,680
"You'll learn."

36
00:01:30,880 --> 00:01:32,670
The president is eating cereal.

37
00:01:32,960 --> 00:01:36,750
This is somehow the most unsettling
thing you have seen all morning.

38
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:41,280
The man whose face covers entire buildings
is arguing with an assistant about a

39
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:42,390
missing banana.

40
00:01:42,740 --> 00:01:44,090
Then he notices you.

41
00:01:44,320 --> 00:01:47,130
He remembers your name,
asks about your mother,

42
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:49,450
even knows which hospital treated her.

43
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:51,430
You feel yourself relax.

44
00:01:51,740 --> 00:01:53,970
Here is someone who actually cares.

45
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:57,410
Then he asks whether your brother
likes his new university.

46
00:01:58,000 --> 00:01:59,710
You never told him you had a brother.

47
00:01:59,980 --> 00:02:01,300
Your shoulders tighten again.

48
00:02:01,340 --> 00:02:04,470
"Welcome to the family," he says.

49
00:02:07,340 --> 00:02:10,310
The first surprise is how
boring the job can be.

50
00:02:10,759 --> 00:02:13,770
People imagine explosions
and heroic dives.

51
00:02:14,100 --> 00:02:16,190
Mostly, you stand beside doors.

52
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:19,990
You learn which floorboards
squeak, which ministers sweat,

53
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:23,970
which meetings run late because the
president enjoys making people wait.

54
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:28,640
You also discover that standing
perfectly still for six hours is a skill

55
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:31,610
apparently invented by
someone who hated knees.

56
00:02:32,120 --> 00:02:36,380
But boredom is dangerous because
the room changes before anything

57
00:02:36,420 --> 00:02:37,570
actually happens.

58
00:02:37,820 --> 00:02:39,350
A conversation stops.

59
00:02:39,540 --> 00:02:41,530
An assistant enters without knocking.

60
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:45,010
Someone who always makes
eye contact suddenly won't.

61
00:02:45,460 --> 00:02:47,190
Your job is to notice.

62
00:02:47,480 --> 00:02:50,430
Your problem is deciding
what any of it means.

63
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:53,950
One afternoon, the president tells a joke.

64
00:02:54,300 --> 00:02:55,390
Everyone laughs.

65
00:02:55,640 --> 00:02:57,990
The finance minister laughs a second late.

66
00:02:58,320 --> 00:03:00,270
At dinner, his chair is empty.

67
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:01,610
Maybe he's sick.

68
00:03:01,820 --> 00:03:03,250
Maybe he's been dismissed.

69
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:05,130
You consider asking Marek.

70
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:07,730
Then you remember your
mother's hospital room.

71
00:03:08,140 --> 00:03:09,090
You eat your dinner.

72
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:12,950
Six months in, your salary doubles.

73
00:03:13,220 --> 00:03:14,610
Nobody explains why.

74
00:03:14,940 --> 00:03:16,770
You buy your father a new car.

75
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:21,050
He walks around it three times, touching
the paint like it might disappear.

76
00:03:21,380 --> 00:03:22,890
He tells you he's proud.

77
00:03:23,180 --> 00:03:26,230
That feels better than anything
the president has ever said.

78
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:28,770
For a moment, the job makes sense.

79
00:03:29,660 --> 00:03:31,030
Then your phone rings.

80
00:03:31,260 --> 00:03:32,510
"Dinner at the palace.

81
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:35,070
Immediately." It's your
daughter's birthday.

82
00:03:35,360 --> 00:03:37,790
You explain that you'll only
be gone a little while.

83
00:03:38,080 --> 00:03:40,590
She asks whether you'll be
back before the candles.

84
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:41,770
You say yes.

85
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:45,850
At midnight, you return
to a dark apartment.

86
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:48,110
A slice of cake waits in the fridge.

87
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:49,850
Your daughter has left a note.

88
00:03:50,140 --> 00:03:51,430
"We saved your piece."

89
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:56,090
You stand there in your expensive
suit, eating it with your fingers.

90
00:03:59,080 --> 00:04:00,580
Marek notices the next morning.

91
00:04:00,620 --> 00:04:03,450
"Never promise a time," he says.

92
00:04:03,760 --> 00:04:05,310
You ask how he manages it.

93
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:07,730
He shows you a photograph of a little boy.

94
00:04:07,960 --> 00:04:08,950
"My grandson."

95
00:04:09,340 --> 00:04:10,730
You didn't know he had one.

96
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:12,330
"Does he want to be a soldier?"

97
00:04:12,680 --> 00:04:14,490
Marek puts the photograph away.

98
00:04:14,760 --> 00:04:16,329
"He wants to be a dentist."

99
00:04:16,579 --> 00:04:18,580
For the first time, you hear him laugh.

100
00:04:18,620 --> 00:04:20,470
"A sensible man."

101
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:22,490
After that, you trust him,

102
00:04:23,440 --> 00:04:26,370
which makes the following
winter considerably worse.

103
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:29,930
You arrive at work and find
a stranger in his office.

104
00:04:30,240 --> 00:04:31,670
Marek has been arrested.

105
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:35,250
The announcement says he passed
information to foreign agents.

106
00:04:35,520 --> 00:04:37,930
At breakfast, the
president shakes his head.

107
00:04:38,140 --> 00:04:40,190
"After everything I did for him."

108
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:41,550
Then he looks at you.

109
00:04:41,820 --> 00:04:43,030
"Did you notice anything?"

110
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:46,010
Your mind fills with conversations.

111
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:48,270
The elevator, the photograph.

112
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:52,220
Every harmless complaint now sounds
different when you imagine someone writing

113
00:04:52,260 --> 00:04:53,060
it down.

114
00:04:53,220 --> 00:04:54,580
You remember his third rule.

115
00:04:54,620 --> 00:04:57,490
"Tell me before you tell anyone else."

116
00:04:57,780 --> 00:05:00,100
Was that protection or something else?

117
00:05:00,140 --> 00:05:02,490
"I don't know anything, sir."

118
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:07,990
The president watches you for another
second, then he returns to his breakfast.

119
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:10,830
You never see Marek again.

120
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:15,110
By your third year,

121
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:18,410
you know the president better than
some members of your own family.

122
00:05:18,760 --> 00:05:22,570
You know when he is tired, when
he is pretending to be angry,

123
00:05:22,900 --> 00:05:24,690
when he is actually afraid.

124
00:05:25,340 --> 00:05:28,610
Tonight, at a televised
banquet, he seems relaxed.

125
00:05:28,900 --> 00:05:32,430
There are diplomats, business
leaders, senior officers.

126
00:05:32,780 --> 00:05:34,610
You stand behind his right shoulder.

127
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:36,410
A server brings a drink.

128
00:05:36,760 --> 00:05:40,590
The president is talking, so you take
the glass and place it within reach.

129
00:05:41,260 --> 00:05:43,010
He drinks, laughs,

130
00:05:43,900 --> 00:05:44,850
then stops.

131
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:46,770
His hand grips the table.

132
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:48,730
A chair scrapes backward.

133
00:05:49,020 --> 00:05:49,820
You move.

134
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:51,430
Someone shouts your name.

135
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:53,310
Another guard grabs your arm.

136
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:55,890
You pull free and call
for the medical team.

137
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:57,810
Everything becomes noise.

138
00:05:58,060 --> 00:05:59,550
The president collapses.

139
00:05:59,860 --> 00:06:01,750
Guests stumble over chairs.

140
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:03,250
You kneel beside him.

141
00:06:03,520 --> 00:06:06,150
For a moment, his eyes lock onto yours.

142
00:06:06,380 --> 00:06:07,810
He looks terrified.

143
00:06:08,168 --> 00:06:10,218
You stay until the doctors take over.

144
00:06:10,468 --> 00:06:12,398
Then someone pulls you to your feet.

145
00:06:12,628 --> 00:06:14,878
They take your weapon and your phone.

146
00:06:16,248 --> 00:06:17,898
You wait nine hours.

147
00:06:18,188 --> 00:06:20,178
Nobody tells you whether he is alive.

148
00:06:20,588 --> 00:06:22,898
Finally, a security officer enters.

149
00:06:23,128 --> 00:06:25,098
He places a photograph on the table.

150
00:06:25,428 --> 00:06:27,238
You handing over the glass.

151
00:06:27,548 --> 00:06:28,558
"Explain this."

152
00:06:29,048 --> 00:06:29,848
So you do.

153
00:06:30,188 --> 00:06:31,838
Then you explain it again.

154
00:06:32,148 --> 00:06:35,898
By the fifth time, you are trying to
remember whether you touched the rim.

155
00:06:36,248 --> 00:06:39,818
By the tenth, you are questioning
details you were certain about.

156
00:06:40,168 --> 00:06:41,418
The officer leaves.

157
00:06:41,668 --> 00:06:43,278
You stare at the photograph.

158
00:06:43,588 --> 00:06:47,818
One ordinary movement, frozen
at exactly the wrong moment.

159
00:06:49,168 --> 00:06:51,418
The next morning, the
president summons you.

160
00:06:51,648 --> 00:06:53,978
He is sitting up in bed, alive.

161
00:06:54,608 --> 00:06:55,558
He smiles.

162
00:06:55,808 --> 00:06:57,398
"They tell me you acted quickly."

163
00:06:57,808 --> 00:07:00,598
Relief hits so hard you almost fall over.

164
00:07:00,928 --> 00:07:02,718
He gestures toward a television.

165
00:07:02,988 --> 00:07:06,708
The news announces that security
services have defeated an assassination

166
00:07:06,748 --> 00:07:07,548
attempt.

167
00:07:07,728 --> 00:07:10,278
Several conspirators
are already in custody.

168
00:07:10,588 --> 00:07:11,738
You ask what happened.

169
00:07:11,988 --> 00:07:13,458
The president doesn't answer.

170
00:07:13,708 --> 00:07:16,378
Instead, he says, "You'll
receive a medal."

171
00:07:16,788 --> 00:07:18,518
Then his expression changes.

172
00:07:18,788 --> 00:07:22,138
"For the cameras, you noticed a
suspicious man near the table."

173
00:07:22,508 --> 00:07:23,378
You hesitate.

174
00:07:23,608 --> 00:07:24,958
You didn't notice anyone.

175
00:07:26,068 --> 00:07:26,868
He waits.

176
00:07:27,128 --> 00:07:29,578
On the bedside table is a list of names.

177
00:07:29,728 --> 00:07:30,898
You recognize one,

178
00:07:31,688 --> 00:07:32,488
Marek.

179
00:07:32,648 --> 00:07:34,298
"Of course, sir," you say.

180
00:07:35,468 --> 00:07:37,298
The ceremony airs that evening.

181
00:07:37,448 --> 00:07:38,838
Your father records it.

182
00:07:39,048 --> 00:07:41,218
Your daughter tells her
friends you're a hero.

183
00:07:41,548 --> 00:07:44,358
You watch yourself describe
a man you never saw.

184
00:07:45,308 --> 00:07:49,098
Three days later, you receive a
promotion, a bigger apartment,

185
00:07:49,228 --> 00:07:52,958
a higher salary, and a desk
far away from the president.

186
00:07:53,748 --> 00:07:57,958
Your replacement is twenty-six,
new suit, perfect posture.

187
00:07:58,228 --> 00:08:00,198
He asks whether you have any advice.

188
00:08:00,488 --> 00:08:02,418
You think about telling him everything.

189
00:08:02,708 --> 00:08:04,778
Instead, you straighten his tie.

190
00:08:04,968 --> 00:08:09,278
His phone lights up, a message from
his mother, "We're so proud of you."

191
00:08:09,488 --> 00:08:10,958
You let go of the tie.

192
00:08:11,248 --> 00:08:13,618
"Don't promise your family
what time you'll be home."

193
00:08:15,008 --> 00:08:17,498
That night, your daughter
asks to see the medal.

194
00:08:17,828 --> 00:08:19,578
She turns it over in her hands.

195
00:08:19,888 --> 00:08:20,858
"Were you scared?"

196
00:08:21,188 --> 00:08:22,318
You tell her, "Yes."

197
00:08:22,608 --> 00:08:24,078
"But you saved him anyway."

198
00:08:24,408 --> 00:08:25,678
You look at the television.

199
00:08:25,928 --> 00:08:29,178
The news is showing photographs
of the supposed conspirators.

200
00:08:29,468 --> 00:08:30,718
You reach for the remote.

201
00:08:30,988 --> 00:08:32,478
Your daughter is still waiting.

202
00:08:32,768 --> 00:08:33,748
You switch off the screen.

203
00:08:33,788 --> 00:08:36,318
"Yes," you say,

204
00:08:37,248 --> 00:08:39,918
and you let her believe that
was the difficult part.
